{{- /*
The `jj log` arguments the fish, bash and zsh prompts read a jj workspace's
state with, after `jj --no-integrate-operation status` has snapshotted it.
Include after `jj log`, with --at-op set to that snapshot's operation when it
made one (--at-op implies --ignore-working-copy, which is here for when not):

  command jj --at-op=<op> log {{ includeTemplate "jj-prompt" }} </dev/null 2>/dev/null

The lines end in a backslash and the words are single-quoted with a backslash
inside only before " and n, all of which fish and sh read the same way, so jj
sees the same text from either.

It prints one line per fact, from whichever commits they're about:

  w <change id> <flags>  @: * changes but no description, ! conflict,
                         ? divergent
  b <bookmark>...        the nearest commits at or below @ with bookmarks
  t                      the tip, @ unless it's empty and undescribed, then @-,
                         isn't on a remote bookmark (one line per parent)
  r                      a remote bookmark exists, so pushing means something
*/ -}}
--ignore-working-copy --no-graph --color=never \
-r '@ | heads(::@ & bookmarks()) | coalesce(@ ~ (empty() & description(exact:"")), @-) | latest(remote_bookmarks())' \
-T 'concat(
  if(current_working_copy, "w " ++ change_id.shortest() ++ " " ++ concat(
    if(!empty && description == "", "*"),
    if(conflict, "!"),
    if(divergent, "?"),
  ) ++ "\n"),
  if(self.contained_in("heads(::@ & bookmarks())"),
    "b " ++ local_bookmarks.map(|b| b.name()).join(" ") ++ "\n"),
  if(self.contained_in("coalesce(@ ~ (empty() & description(exact:\"\")), @-) ~ ::remote_bookmarks()"),
    "t\n"),
  if(self.contained_in("remote_bookmarks()"), "r\n"),
)'